  "repo_truth": "Review 6 admitted the exact 26-path subject and returned one planning-versus-implementation status Nit. The parent accepted it without waiver. This exact 27-path subject attaches review-clean only to the Option 1 planning handoff and states separately that the selected implementation stopped without clean implementation review. Every previously frozen identity, intent 1.2 byte, exact terminal label, collision, fsync, scratch, recovery, immutable-source, verified-snapshot, Rust-scope, and HCM-2.3 stop rule is unchanged.",
  "allowed_scope": ["Remain read-only and replay all 27 manifest hashes/order/aggregate before review.", "Independently review the entire complete identity/currentness/persistence/recovery subject, not only Review 6 remediation.", "Adversarially verify the planning-versus-implementation status boundary, exact terminal-axis labels, immutable historical-source support, both four-state terminal destination axes/negatives, terminal-marker fsync replay, transaction-keyed journals, whole-file scratch publication, 36+8 fault products, W0-W15/R0-R9, collision and mismatch preservation.", "Return findings first with exact evidence, failure mode, smallest repair, and missing validation."],
  "non_goals": ["No edits, staging, commits, handoff/ledger writes, snapshot mutation, or user task hops.", "No Rust/test work, implementation resumption, schema widening, fallback/dual read, relaxed validation, prior-evidence rewrite, HCM-2.3 work, or adjacent cleanup.", "Do not inherit prior verdicts; derive the whole result independently."],
  "tasks": ["Invoke ordered skills and return BLOCKED on any manifest mismatch.", "Verify the complete identity graph, schemas/vectors, source support, status authority, persistence, currentness, writer/recovery, collisions, mismatch, fsync, and fault grammar.", "Prove the review-clean classification belongs only to the planning subject; both terminal axes use the exact machine labels; only absent destinations rename; every collision preserves pending; all whole-file/fsync/path/fault rules remain complete; and scratch never enters recovery.", "Replay historical research claims from immutable Git objects and distinguish them from repaired mutable current state.", "Return CLEAN only with no Critical, Required, Optional, or Nit finding; otherwise CHANGES_REQUIRED or BLOCKED without repair."],
  "contracts_and_gates": ["docs/specs/handbook-contract-membrane/slices/HCM-2.2/SPEC.md#promotion-transaction-intent-12-and-recovery", "docs/specs/handbook-contract-membrane/slices/HCM-2.2/contracts/promotion-transaction-intent-1.2.0.schema.json", "docs/specs/handbook-contract-membrane/slices/HCM-2.2/contracts/promotion-transaction-intent-vectors-v1.0.json", "docs/specs/handbook-contract-membrane/slices/HCM-2.2/proof/20260720T223544Z--atomic-stage-review-6-remediation-proof.md", "docs/specs/handbook-contract-membrane/06-proof-and-regression-ledger.md#hcm-22-constitutional-root-implementation-proof-gate"],
